Contents of "s:" directory...

    user-startup

        - Contains all ASSIGNS pertaining to FIDO and JAMMAIL that I am
          currently using, as well as the PATH statement additions.

    call
    JamMail.cfg2
    JamMail.Wpl2
    killjam
    setup2
    setup.cli2

        - First, DO NOT EXPECT these config files to work on YOUR system.
          I'm running a single line system off a SupraFax, v32bis 14.4 modem.
          I am only running FIDO-Net, with no UUCP or other networks online.
          I do NOT use the automatic "Atomic Clock" features or the GPFAX
          features. Presently, this config works FINE on MY system, but may
          need some further modifications on YOUR part to work successfully.

        - I included these files ONLY BECAUSE I have read over numerous posts
          and responses asking why other peoples configs weren't working.
          MAYBE these files will give you some insight into figuring out the
          problem on your system. They are meant to be LOOKED at, and not
          actually used, which is why I appended the "2" to the filenames, so
          you do not mistakenly copy them on top of one of your files.

        - The "call" file was not modified from it's original form as found
          in the "jm950114.lha" archive. It's included here only so you can
          make sure it exists in YOUR S: directory, as JamMail uses it with
          it's CALL command.

        - The "killjam" script was written by me. JamMail creates a "killjm"
          script which will close down JamMail, but I noticed that it does
          NOT close down the Log Window. My "killjam" script closes this one
          down as well. Only running one line through JamMail, it closes only
          the Line 1 window. If your JamMail loads more than one line, you'll
          need to add to this script to close down other line windows.

        - Lastly, make sure the SCRIPT BIT is set on both the "killjam" and
          the "setup" files, else they won't function correctly.

